docker run -p 8888:8888 config-server
i am getting below error
Unsatisfied dependency expressed through method 'searchPathCompositeEnvironmentRepository' parameter 0: Error creating bean with name 'defaultEnvironmentRepository' defined in class path resource [org/springframework/cloud/config/server/config/DefaultRepositoryConfiguration.class]: You need to configure a uri for the git repository.
2026-01-13T05:23:12.413Z  INFO 1 --- [config] [           main] o.apache.catalina.core.StandardService   : Stopping service [Tomcat]
2026-01-13T05:23:12.460Z  INFO 1 --- [config] [           main] .s.b.a.l.ConditionEvaluationReportLogger :

Error starting ApplicationContext. To display the condition evaluation report re-run your application with 'debug' enabled.
2026-01-13T05:23:12.505Z ERROR 1 --- [config] [           main] o.s.b.d.LoggingFailureAnalysisReporter   :

***************************
APPLICATION FAILED TO START
***************************

Description:

Invalid config server configuration.

Action:

If you are using the git profile, you need to set a Git URI in your configuration.  If you have set spring.cloud.config.server.bootstrap=true, you need to use a composite configuration.

***********************************************************************
solution:
This error is expected behavior 👍 — your Config Server is starting correctly, but Spring Cloud Config Server must know where to read configuration files from.

Right now, no backend (Git / Native / Vault etc.) is configured, so it fails at startup.

Use Git Repository (Most Common – Production)
==============================================
server:
  port: 8888

spring:
  cloud:
    config:
      server:
        git:
          uri: https://github.com/your-org/config-repo
          default-label: main
          clone-on-start: true



2️⃣ Rebuild Docker Image And RUN
-----------------------------
mvn clean package
docker build -t config-server .
docker run -p 8888:8888 config-server  --- change it


Test Config Server
http://localhost:8888/students/default
http://localhost:8888/schools/default
http://localhost:8888/discovery/default

***************************************************************
i am getting below error while running gateway service
***************************************************************
    main] c.n.d.s.t.d.RedirectingEurekaHttpClient  :
Request execution error. endpoint=DefaultEndpoint{ serviceUrl='http://localhost:8761/eureka/},
exception=I/O error on GET request for "http://localhost:8761/eureka/apps/":
Connect to http://localhost:8761 [localhost/127.0.0.1, localhost/0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1]
failed: Connection refused stacktrace=org.springframework.web.client.ResourceAccessException:
I/O error on GET request for "http://localhost:8761/eureka/apps/":
Connect to http://localhost:8761 [localhost/127.0.0.1, localhost/0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1] failed:
Connection refused


Solution:
You are NOT explicitly using localhost, but Spring is still trying to call localhost:8761.

Let me explain why this happens, and then give you the exact fix.

Your gateway.yml
eureka:
  client:
    register-with-eureka: false

  You did NOT define:

  eureka.client.service-url.defaultZone

👉 What Spring Does Internally

When defaultZone is not specified, Spring Cloud Netflix uses this DEFAULT value:

http://localhost:8761/eureka
So even though you didn’t write localhost, Spring added it automatically.

That’s exactly why your logs show:

GET http://localhost:8761/eureka/apps/
Connection refused


Key Rule (MEMORIZE)

❗ If Eureka client is on the classpath
❗ And defaultZone is missing
👉 Spring assumes localhost:8761




correct fix:
eureka:
  client:
    register-with-eureka: false
    fetch-registry: false
    service-url:
      defaultZone: http://discovery:8761/eureka



~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~````
After changing gateway.yml do i need to build it again?

NO: You did:

    Changed gateway.yml in Config Server

    Did NOT change:
      Gateway Java code
      Gateway Dockerfile
      Gateway JAR

    👉 That means Docker image has NOT changed.

🧠 Rule of Thumb (Memorize This)
❌ Rebuild NOT required when:

You change config-server config files
You change .yml in Git-backed config repo
You change environment variables via Config Server

✅ Rebuild required ONLY when:

Java code changes
application.yml inside the service changes
pom.xml changes
Dockerfile changes



🧠 Rule to Memorize (Very Important)
-------------------------------------
Change type	Rebuild needed?
------------------------------
application.yml inside service	✅ YES
Java code	✅ YES
pom.xml	✅ YES
Dockerfile	✅ YES
Config Server config (discovery.yml)	❌ NO
Git-backed config repo	❌ NO


